      "description": "Watch Arsenal vs Crystal Palace highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on December 24, 2025. On a high-stakes Christmas Eve at Villa Park, Aston Villa and Arsenal locked horns in a Carabao Cup tie that blended tactical discipline with moments of high drama. Both sides sought to secure a place in the next round as the 2025-12-24 fixture delivered a clash of narrow margins. A Cautious Opening Exchange The first half was characterized by a tactical stalemate and frequent interruptions. Arsenal attempted to establish dominance through possession, but their rhythm was repeatedly broken by the assistant referee's flag, with Kai Havertz and Declan Rice often found in offside positions. Gabriel had a half-chance from a Rice corner, but his header failed to test the goalkeeper. Aston Villa remained competitive but were plagued by unforced defensive errors. Players like Zion Suzuki and John McGinn narrowly avoided gifting opportunities to the visitors. The physical nature of the contest became evident when Christos Tzolis picked up a yellow card for a professional foul to halt a rapid Arsenal counter-attack, leaving the match scoreless at the break. VAR Controversy and the Breakthrough The momentum shifted dramatically early in the second half. In the 54th minute, Ian Maatsen was judged to have fouled Bukayo Saka inside the area, prompting the referee to point to the penalty spot. However, after a lengthy VAR review, the decision was overturned, briefly handing the initiative back to the hosts. Undeterred, Arsenal found their breakthrough in the 59th minute. A brilliant sequence involving Eberechi Eze allowed Riccardo Calafiori to provide a pinpoint assist for Bukayo Saka . The winger made no mistake, firing home with his left foot to give the Gunners a crucial lead. It was a goal that reflected Arsenal's 61% possession dominance throughout the match. Late Tension and Tactical Shifts As the clock ticked down, Aston Villa introduced Alejandro Garnacho and Tammy Abraham in a desperate search for an equalizer. Despite late pressure and several corners won by Emiliano Buendía , the Arsenal defense held firm. Tactical substitutions, including the introduction of Martin Zubimendi and Mikel Merino , helped the visitors navigate the final stages. The closing moments were marred by a flurry of bookings for the home side, with Alysson Edward , John McGinn , and Ian Maatsen all entering the referee's book. In front of an attendance of 36,804, Arsenal successfully managed the final minutes to secure their victory and progression in the tournament."
